WEBVTT

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:48.420
Gently now, gently...

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:57.330
What happened?

00:01:57.330 --> 00:01:59.800
They said Kiyoko collapsed.

00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:11.610
It's excessive stress.

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:16.080
I see. She's more fragile than I thought.

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:20.150
With two or three days of rest, she should be fine.

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:24.160
Doctor...

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:25.190
Yes?

00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:27.990
As a precaution, won't you check something for me?

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:29.990
What might that be?

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:23.270
My lady sends word bidding you all have breakfast without her.

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:25.380
I see.

00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:44.400
Well, then, let's eat.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:45.730
Let's eat.

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:59.110
Are you worried about your sister?

00:03:59.990 --> 00:04:01.380
No...

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:10.520
It's unusual for that woman not to be at breakfast,

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:14.890
...since having meals together is our one and only rule here.

00:04:15.830 --> 00:04:17.230
It is?

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:21.100
She says eating meals together makes a family.

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:26.830
She thinks of us as family. You too, and your sister.

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:31.170
She tries to fit everything into her imagined mold.

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:33.310
It's a bad habit of hers.

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:36.590
She herself is aware of it, but she still does it.

00:04:48.570 --> 00:04:50.770
So who is she?

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:54.900
Just a widow with time on her hands. Doesn't cover it, does it?

00:04:55.810 --> 00:04:57.870
The fact is, I don't really know.

00:04:58.410 --> 00:05:01.110
But she's a substitute mother to us, of sorts.

00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:04.210
You and the others were scouted, right?

00:05:05.350 --> 00:05:08.790
The same as you two, we were bought with money.

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:13.920
All of us in our own way are carrying around some kind of dark past,

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:16.620
...though we don't show it in our manner.

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:22.690
When all's said and done, fighting Gilgamesh is...

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:24.660
Just killing time?

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:28.170
That's right.

00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:34.810
How about working up a sweat with some post-breakfast exercise?

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:47.650
Not bad.

00:05:59.770 --> 00:06:01.800
Yeah, that's the way.

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:06.270
Try doing something like you just did.

00:06:11.650 --> 00:06:13.580
Absurdly easy, huh?

00:06:14.050 --> 00:06:16.890
You can go along learning a little at a time like this.

00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:20.060
Even if you don't use it in battle,

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:22.120
...you may be able to make money on the street.

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:30.570
Let's have a four-person snowball fight. Us against you.

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:34.130
That's no fair. Both of you are bigger!

00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:37.800
One of us is a beginner, it evens out.

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:07.470
What did you come here for?

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:11.040
It's because I was concerned about you.

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:14.370
Was that kind of examination necessary?

00:07:15.150 --> 00:07:17.770
If we waited to find out, it would be too late, right?

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:20.640
There's no way that kind of thing could've happened!

00:07:20.950 --> 00:07:24.720
I've told you a number of times what happened there.

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:29.850
We're dealing with Gilgamesh. We need caution upon caution.

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:34.190
I was thinking of you when I did this.

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:40.210
Hearing the report was a bit surprising.

00:07:40.210 --> 00:07:44.770
You never have, have you? I was thinking you had played around a bit.

00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:48.810
Is there something wrong with that?

00:07:49.010 --> 00:07:50.950
How could there be something wrong with it?

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:54.990
If you weren't reliable, it would be a lost cause.

00:07:54.990 --> 00:07:56.580
With that mother...

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:01.150
Slovenly, filthy, unsightly, and alcohol-sodden...

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:04.530
So you made inquiries?

00:08:04.530 --> 00:08:07.230
A natural thing to do, as a creditor.

00:08:07.730 --> 00:08:10.530
Apparently you've had it awfully hard, since you were little.

00:08:11.140 --> 00:08:13.040
After your mother's passing,

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:16.130
...your life was nothing but running away with your little brother.

00:08:17.340 --> 00:08:22.680
And in the end, you were captured by a cruel woman and caged like a bird.

00:08:23.210 --> 00:08:25.720
At a time like that, I wonder if you might not be enraptured...

00:08:25.720 --> 00:08:28.980
...by kind words spoken by a good-looking boy?

00:08:30.050 --> 00:08:31.820
What is it you want to say?

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:34.830
I'm still suspicious...

00:08:34.830 --> 00:08:38.850
...about whether you went with them of your own will.

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:43.490
Please don't talk nonsense. That would never happen.

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:46.140
I hope not.

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:05.590
Since then, your brother has been steadily learning to use Dynamis.

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:08.620
He's beginning to accept his own destiny.

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:12.460
I'm very aware that I'm willfully having my own say,

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:15.100
...but let me say just one thing.

00:09:15.100 --> 00:09:17.730
Just do not get in our way.

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:32.240
Can you do this?

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:46.520
Give it a try.

00:10:08.590 --> 00:10:10.350
Maybe that's still too hard.

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:17.120
Fu!

00:10:19.400 --> 00:10:21.070
Me?

00:10:21.070 --> 00:10:23.800
He won't be as glad to have me do it, right?

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:38.210
A nosebleed!

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:43.550
Fuko...

00:10:43.550 --> 00:10:45.320
Go a little easy on him!

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:50.960
The first time Fujisaki did it to me, I was bleeding and stuff too.

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:02.960
Are you all right?

00:11:03.540 --> 00:11:04.940
Yeah...

00:11:04.940 --> 00:11:06.740
Then give it a try.

00:11:17.620 --> 00:11:19.150
He did it!

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:21.150
Send it over there.

00:11:31.240 --> 00:11:33.360
This time we'll have a snowball fight like that.

00:11:33.840 --> 00:11:35.670
Using your hands is a foul.

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:38.010
If we're gonna do that, let's make a smokescreen.

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:07.700
Miss Kiyoko, how are you feeling?

00:13:07.870 --> 00:13:11.430
I'm fine now. I'm sorry for making you worry.

00:13:11.940 --> 00:13:13.930
Oh no, no need whatsoever for apologies.

00:13:15.310 --> 00:13:17.540
Say, where's my brother?

00:13:17.540 --> 00:13:20.240
He went into the courtyard a little while ago with Isamu and the others.

00:13:42.430 --> 00:13:43.800
Shuffle.

00:13:57.450 --> 00:13:59.010
Providence!

00:14:13.060 --> 00:14:14.620
Kiyoko!

00:15:04.720 --> 00:15:08.340
Tatsuya learned to use Dynamis pretty well today.

00:15:09.350 --> 00:15:12.090
It's because he's obedient and absorbs things quickly.

00:15:12.090 --> 00:15:15.180
I see. Being obedient is the best thing after all.

00:15:16.660 --> 00:15:19.060
You've gotten good control over your table manners, too,

00:15:19.530 --> 00:15:22.090
...although at first I didn't know what would come of them.

00:15:22.630 --> 00:15:24.900
That's because everyone's taught me.

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:27.030
Elegance is important.

00:15:28.310 --> 00:15:30.470
Is Kiyoko still not well?

00:15:31.980 --> 00:15:34.010
She seems much better.

00:15:34.010 --> 00:15:35.510
You're worried, aren't you?

00:15:35.510 --> 00:15:36.780
Yeah...

00:15:37.050 --> 00:15:38.950
Yeah, you really care about her a lot.

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:43.220
You kept glancing up toward the infirmary even while we were having the snowball fight.

00:15:43.550 --> 00:15:44.790
I did not!

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:46.220
Yes, you did.

00:15:46.220 --> 00:15:49.060
So you thought nobody could tell in the middle of all that.

00:15:49.060 --> 00:15:51.090
You still need a lot more training.

00:15:52.400 --> 00:15:56.560
Tatsuya, you've got kind of a sister complex, huh?

00:15:57.000 --> 00:15:58.900
Kiyoko IS pretty.

00:15:59.500 --> 00:16:00.970
That's taking it too far.

00:16:01.410 --> 00:16:05.570
With the hard experiences he's had in getting this far, it's only natural.

00:16:06.010 --> 00:16:08.440
He'd deserve punishment if he didn't feel that way.

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:12.580
Tatsuya's caring. I like caring children.

00:16:14.090 --> 00:16:16.290
Family is an irreplaceable thing.

00:16:16.290 --> 00:16:18.880
Though admittedly temporary, we're a family too.

00:16:19.190 --> 00:16:21.850
Eating meals together makes a family.

00:16:22.390 --> 00:16:25.230
That's why I take this sort of setting so seriously.

00:16:26.200 --> 00:16:28.720
So, Countess, you're the mother?

00:16:29.400 --> 00:16:33.300
That's how it works out. You must be glad your mother's so beautiful!

00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:52.650
Is it okay for you to be up?

00:16:53.060 --> 00:16:54.520
Yeah...

00:16:57.060 --> 00:16:58.960
Hey, Tatsuya...

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:01.300
Yeah?

00:17:01.300 --> 00:17:03.790
Which is better, now or before?

00:17:05.070 --> 00:17:06.590
What do you mean, which is better?

00:17:07.170 --> 00:17:10.630
Before, we were always afraid, wondering when we'd be caught.

00:17:12.280 --> 00:17:16.110
I thought I wanted to get away from that life, the sooner the better.

00:17:18.280 --> 00:17:20.110
We've gotten out of it, for now.

00:17:21.120 --> 00:17:24.610
At least we weren't slaves though.

00:17:25.060 --> 00:17:27.960
We're not slaves or anything...

00:17:29.260 --> 00:17:31.160
So you're not aware of it.

00:17:31.660 --> 00:17:33.760
Well, what are you saying we should do?

00:17:37.030 --> 00:17:38.590
Run away from here?

00:17:43.210 --> 00:17:45.510
That would be impossible.

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:48.840
We don't know that, unless we try.

00:17:49.450 --> 00:17:51.310
I know it even without trying.

00:17:52.420 --> 00:17:54.040
So you don't have the nerve, huh?

00:17:54.390 --> 00:17:58.320
Maybe not, but that's not all.

00:17:59.060 --> 00:18:00.190
What, then?

00:18:00.190 --> 00:18:04.990
I don't know how to say it, but in order to face Dad, I think it's better to stay here.

00:18:06.230 --> 00:18:07.890
To face Dad?

00:18:08.530 --> 00:18:09.860
Mom said it too, right?

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:14.170
That she didn't understand why a man like our father would do something like that.

00:18:14.170 --> 00:18:17.040
That there's no way he would have done it.

00:18:17.040 --> 00:18:21.910
Who cares what Mom said? It's that woman's fault we suffered so much.

00:18:22.750 --> 00:18:25.540
I think the one who had it the hardest is you.

00:18:26.020 --> 00:18:31.510
All I had to do was rely on you, and in the end Mom escaped into the booze.

00:18:32.320 --> 00:18:35.120
I'm really grateful to you, Kiyoko.

00:18:36.260 --> 00:18:37.730
What's this all about?

00:18:39.230 --> 00:18:45.500
After spending the day today with those kids, I thought maybe I can do something too!

00:18:46.700 --> 00:18:51.570
If I have the same powers as those kids, this time I can protect you.

00:18:52.540 --> 00:18:55.310
I don't especially want you to protect me or anything.

00:18:56.850 --> 00:18:58.840
What, exactly, do you mean by facing Dad?

00:18:59.550 --> 00:19:01.580
You need to know yourself better.

00:19:02.150 --> 00:19:04.310
Just because you can use magic a little...

00:19:04.520 --> 00:19:05.920
Kiyoko...

00:19:06.820 --> 00:19:09.860
You're timid by nature, so stop thinking up these outrageous things.

00:19:09.860 --> 00:19:14.890
You, who when you get scared immediately start peeing blood.

00:19:15.670 --> 00:19:17.430
Why are you bringing that up now?!

00:19:19.770 --> 00:19:23.800
You'd only be a hindrance to those kids. Give it up.

00:19:25.980 --> 00:19:29.340
Listen, Tatsuya, you're still a child.

00:19:29.850 --> 00:19:32.480
You just need to be quiet and do what your sister says.

00:19:33.120 --> 00:19:36.140
I'm thinking of your own good when I say that.

00:19:36.990 --> 00:19:40.920
Stop trying to treat me like a child forever! And on top of that...

00:19:42.090 --> 00:19:44.430
On top of that? What?

00:19:44.430 --> 00:19:47.920
The way you said that sounded like the Countess somehow.

00:19:50.900 --> 00:19:53.270
How am I like that woman?

00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:56.130
Because that's how you sounded.

00:19:59.480 --> 00:20:00.910
That's horrible!

00:20:01.110 --> 00:20:01.980
Why?!

00:20:01.980 --> 00:20:03.540
Stop!

00:20:04.050 --> 00:20:05.480
Cut it out!

00:20:05.820 --> 00:20:07.280
I said quit it!

00:20:09.050 --> 00:20:10.750
Stop it!

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:32.430
May I?

00:20:33.140 --> 00:20:34.630
Yes...

00:20:35.280 --> 00:20:37.880
Is there some sort of trouble?

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:40.010
No, it's nothing.

00:20:40.550 --> 00:20:45.390
It's late at night. We do not wish to inconvenience the other guests.

00:20:45.390 --> 00:20:46.860
We're sorry.

00:20:47.520 --> 00:20:49.030
Goodnight, then.

00:20:49.030 --> 00:20:50.580
Goodnight.

00:21:21.760 --> 00:21:23.160
Kiyoko did?

00:21:23.160 --> 00:21:24.630
Yes, my lady.

00:21:24.630 --> 00:21:26.390
And what about Tatsuya?

00:23:24.750 --> 00:23:29.520
I was very worried that you might do something to Tatsuya.

00:23:29.520 --> 00:23:31.790
You're not a child anymore either.

00:23:31.790 --> 00:23:33.760
It's because when you looked at him,

00:23:33.760 --> 00:23:35.560
...your eyes looked, how can I say it, deviant.

00:23:35.560 --> 00:23:36.660
You said it yourself, Tatsuya.

00:23:36.660 --> 00:23:39.500
I thought I'd give you a warning, as his sister,

00:23:39.500 --> 00:23:40.760
...so nothing like that happens.

00:23:40.760 --> 00:23:42.300
You jerk, now I'm all wet.

00:23:42.300 --> 00:23:45.600
You always do that: try to control people by intimidation.

00:23:45.600 --> 00:23:46.900
I did get away.

00:23:46.900 --> 00:23:49.070
...said you're going to stay here and face Dad.

00:23:49.070 --> 00:23:50.070
But I don't want to.

00:23:50.070 --> 00:23:51.110
That stupid Tatsuya!

00:23:51.110 --> 00:23:51.980
Bonehead!

00:23:51.980 --> 00:23:54.000
We won't be lonely or anything, you know.
